## Kubernetes

Use `datus k8s` for namespace-scoped Kubernetes workload inspection, logs,
events, metrics, manifests, rollout status/restart, scaling, and running a
single non-interactive `exec` probe in
a pod. The command surface is kubectl-style but intentionally excludes
cluster-scoped resources, all-namespaces access, interactive exec/attach, cp,
port forwarding, and kubeconfig mutation.

Use bounded, individual `get` calls to re-check asynchronous resources so every
observation returns control to the agent. Read focused status fields with
`-o jsonpath={.path.to.field}` and inspect `status.error`, conditions, pods, and
warning events before deciding whether to retry.

